###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# No training or inference times are given. Thermal-expansion and heat-
# capacity MD used 432-atom cells for 100,000 steps of 1 fs.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The MPtrj subset is a random 10% of the data set the universal models were trained on, so it is not a held-out split; the role is left unset. Energy RMSEs stated in eV/atom are converted to meV/atom.
# - The CHG2-FT binding-energy errors are attributed to the CHG2 model with only the convolution layers trainable, which the paper names the best CHG2 model and calls CHG2-FT; MACE-FT is the multi-head replay model. Their Fe-property errors (vacancy energies, grain-boundary and surface energies, Tables 1, 2 and 4) are properties and are not encoded.
# - Learning rates 0.01 and 0.001 (Fig. 4) and the CHGNet freezing variants of Table 3 (Fig. 10) are figure-only. CHGNet 0.3.0 and SevenNet-0 fine-tuned results of Table 4 are properties only. The SevenNet-0 version is not stated, so it is a paper-local run.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/mohandas2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

